##

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:04.120 position:72% line:91%
This video is sponsored by CuriosityStream
and by my Nebula Original. More on that later.

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:06.340 line:91%
Also, the shots are going to look
a little weird, a little wide,

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:09.140 position:64% line:91%
because it is the start of September 2020
as we record this,

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:12.640 position:61% line:91%
and we're following all the UK industry
regulations for filming COVID-safe.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.580 line:85%
All right. Enjoy the show!

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:19.580 position:70% line:91%
In 1927, Helene Adelaide Shelby
of Oakland, California, applied for a patent:

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:23.960 position:75% line:91%
"An apparatus for obtaining criminal confessions
and photographically recording them."

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:25.800 line:85%
It was basically a lie detector.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.740 position:58% line:91%
If you "knew" the suspect was guilty,
but you couldn't prove it,

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:31.360 line:85%
you would use a device like this,

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:34.520 position:59% line:91%
which as far as I know was never built
and never used, until now.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:36.880 line:91%
I have commissioned
my friend Charles to make one.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.280 position:59% line:85%
We've updated some of the technology —

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:40.720 position:56% line:91%
we're using a modern camera
instead of bulky reel-to-reel film —

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.060 line:91%
but this is as true to the patent
as we could make it,

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:48.720 position:63% line:91%
and we're going to test out Ms. Shelby's
lie detector for the very first time.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:52.340 align:end position:100% line:91%
Daniel, Tom, Chloe,
thank you very much for coming along.

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:55.760 align:end position:100% line:85%
We're going to test a 1927 lie detector today.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:57.980 line:91%
<c.yellow>Sure.</c>
<c.cyan>'Cause why not?</c>

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:00.820 position:58% line:85%
I haven't told you all anything else.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.600 line:91%
<c.cyan>There's a lot of trust
in this room, isn't there(?)</c>

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:06.580 line:85%
I'm not feeling it!

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:10.140 position:56% line:91%
<c.yellow>I hope it's not based on heart rate,
'cause I am anxious now!</c>

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:14.940 line:91%
Here's the plan: there is a cookie
on the table, just here.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.460 line:91%
I'm going to leave the room.
One of you steal the cookie.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:20.340 line:85%
<c.yellow>I miss him already.</c>

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:22.700 position:56% line:91%
<c.yellow>There was never any doubt in my mind
that it has to be you.</c>

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:26.800 line:91%
<c.color77FF77>Oh no, not all of you—</c>
<c.yellow>You are the best liar out of us.</c>

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:31.200 line:91%
Alright, so the cookie's gone,
and you all have water bottles now.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:34.320 position:64% line:91%
Which, I feel like one of you went to get
some water after eating the cookie,

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:36.860 line:91%
and then the other two were like,
"We should all have water now."

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:38.380 line:85%
<c.cyan>It's an interesting theory, Watson.</c>

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:40.200 line:85%
I'm not Holmes here — Watson.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.620 position:61% line:91%
The sidekick who doesn't know anything.
Thank you(!)

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:45.500 position:58% line:91%
All right, I'm gonna start over here.
Chloe, did you take the cookie?

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:46.660 line:85%
<c.color77FF77>No.</c>

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.080 line:91%
...Tom, did you take the cookie?
<c.yellow>No.</c>

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:55.120 line:91%
I don't know why, for some reason,
I didn't believe that, but okay.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:59.060 line:91%
Daniel, did you take the cookie?
<c.cyan>No.</c>

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:02.660 position:58% line:85%
Okay, so Chloe I believe immediately.

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:04.740 line:91%
On no evidence.
<c.cyan>How dare you!</c>

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.740 line:91%
I'm not even gonna try and do
an official guess here.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:11.420 position:69% line:91%
My gut reaction is that it's one of you two.
Possibly both of you two.

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:14.020 line:91%
Maybe you split it to try
and trip me up, I don't know.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:19.400 position:61% line:91%
So Chloe, would you please come join me
at the 1927 lie detector?

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:20.900 line:85%
<c.color77FF77>I'd love to.</c>

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:22.980 line:91%
<i>We put Daniel and Tom
in a separate room,</i>

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:26.760 position:69% line:91%
<i>so they couldn't hear Chloe's reaction to...
whatever was inside the box.</i>

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.220 line:85%
<c.color77FF77>Oh, there's two covers, okay.</c>

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:32.340 line:91%
<i>With both those curtains closed,
it was pitch black inside.</i>

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:33.580 line:85%
<c.color77FF77>Oh, very dark.</c>

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:37.240 position:67% line:91%
<i>There was an infrared camera in there,
but Chloe genuinely could not see anything.</i>

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:40.660 position:67% line:91%
<i>So it's probably a good time for earlier-me
to tell you what she's about to face.</i>

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.700 line:91%
<i>Although if you've seen
the title of the video...</i>

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:45.460 line:85%
<i>you've probably worked it out.</i>

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:48.720 line:91%
The problem is that
this lie detector is ridiculous.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:52.240 line:91%
The patent uses very long and
flowery language, but in short...

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:55.180 position:58% line:91%
<i>[whispers]</i> there is a skeleton hidden
at the end of the box!

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:57.940 line:91%
A curtain rises to reveal it,
and the suspect will be startled,

00:02:57.940 --> 00:03:00.960 position:59% line:91%
convinced by this genuine supernatural
apparition from the beyond,

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:03.260 line:91%
which for some reason
will make them confess the truth

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:08.080 position:59% line:91%
as their interrogator asks questions
from behind the box in a spooky voice.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:10.380 line:91%
I'm not kidding.
That's the patent.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:13.300 position:67% line:91%
Ms. Shelby, whoever she was,
never lived to see her invention made real,

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:15.360 line:85%
and perhaps that's for the best.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:19.660 position:59% line:91%
Because patents don't have to be good.
They just have to be new.

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:22.980 line:91%
But with that in mind,
let's try it anyway.

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:26.960 position:61% line:91%
<i>Chloe's first reaction was probably not
what the box's inventor would hope for.</i>

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.580 line:85%
<c.color77FF77><i>[laughs]</i></c>

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:35.320 line:85%
<c.color77FF77>Oh—Oh no.</c>

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:37.080 line:85%
<c.color77FF77>Oh god, it can read into my soul.</c>

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:40.380 line:91%
AS SKELETON:
~Did you take the cookie?~

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:43.680 line:91%
<c.color77FF77>No. I'm sorry.
Was I meant to?</c>

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:46.240 line:85%
~A-A-Are you— Are you sure?~

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:48.520 line:85%
<c.color77FF77>Yes. Unfortunately, yeah.</c>

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:52.540 line:91%
~Thank you. You—
You may leave the box. Woooh!~

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:55.000 line:91%
<c.color77FF77>Oh, okay. Yes, sir.
Thank you, sir.</c>

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.240 line:85%
<c.color77FF77><i>[giggles]</i></c>

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:01.560 line:91%
<i>No confession so far.
So how about Tom?</i>

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:03.060 line:85%
<c.yellow>Cool.</c>

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:06.800 position:67% line:91%
<i>Tom later told me that he has a phobia of
theme park characters and things like this.</i>

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.920 line:85%
<c.yellow>Oh god, oh jeez!</c>

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:12.360 position:70% line:91%
<i>And as he entered the box, he realized that
he'd read about the crime skeleton somewhere.</i>

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:15.360 line:91%
<c.yellow>Oh, I know what this is.
I'm so upset.</c>

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:17.220 line:85%
<i>So first of all, brave!</i>

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:18.440 line:85%
<c.yellow>No...</c>

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:22.080 line:91%
<c.yellow>Oh, there you are!
I knew it.</c>

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:25.600 line:85%
~Did you take the cookie?~

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:28.320 line:91%
<c.yellow>I did not,
mister spooky scary skeleton.</c>

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:31.600 line:91%
~Confess!~
<c.yellow>I didn't, I promise!</c>

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:34.560 line:91%
~Are you sure?~
<c.yellow>I sure am!</c>

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:37.540 position:63% line:85%
~'Cause that's what Chloe said as well.~

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:42.000 position:59% line:91%
<c.yellow>Is this one of those, like,
if I absolve myself, she goes to jail?</c>

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.580 line:91%
<c.yellow>'Cause yeah, she did it.
She totally did it.</c>

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:49.360 line:91%
~Thank you for your time.
You may leave the box.~

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:51.420 line:91%
<c.yellow>Thank you.</c>
~Oooooh!~

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:53.460 line:91%
<c.yellow>You're actually quite nice.
I was quite worried when we met.</c>

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:56.340 line:85%
<c.yellow>But you're surprisingly hospitable.</c>

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:58.800 line:91%
~Please leave the box.~
<c.yellow>Okay.</c>

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:00.740 line:91%
~Please.~
<c.yellow>I'm trying!</c>

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:04.820 line:85%
<c.yellow>That was horrible.</c>

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:08.460 line:91%
<i>Two down, one to go.</i>
<c.cyan>Oh god.</c>

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:10.360 line:85%
<i>Dan was...worried.</i>

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:13.700 line:91%
<c.cyan>Oh my god,
I hate every second of this.</c>

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:16.380 line:85%
<c.cyan>Ugh. Oh, my god.</c>

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:18.900 line:91%
<i>Although I didn't expect
the full-on yell of terror.</i>

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:20.780 line:85%
<c.cyan>Oh my god!</c>

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:22.820 line:85%
<c.cyan>Hi...</c>

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:25.940 line:85%
~Did you take the cookie?~

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:27.520 line:85%
<c.cyan>N-No.</c>

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:29.060 line:85%
~Are you sure?~

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:32.480 line:91%
<c.cyan>I am certain
that I didn't take the cookie.</c>

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:36.720 line:91%
~B-Because that's what
everyone else said. Oooooh!~

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:40.600 position:63% line:91%
<c.cyan>Hmm.</c>
~You definitely didn't take the cookie?~

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:41.920 line:85%
<c.cyan>Was it your cookie?</c>

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:44.700 position:63% line:91%
<c.cyan>'Cause you are looking a little bit like
you could do with a good dinner.</c>

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:48.040 line:91%
~Please leave the box.~
<c.cyan>Okay.</c>

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:51.160 line:85%
<c.cyan>H-How do I get out of the box?</c>

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:53.160 line:85%
~There's curtains you can open.~

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:54.860 line:85%
<c.cyan><i>[chuckles]</i></c>

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:58.740 line:85%
<c.yellow>You better not've talked.</c>

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:00.460 line:85%
So, uh, that didn't work!

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.940 line:91%
That doesn't work at all!
<c.yellow>What?</c>

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:05.780 position:66% line:91%
<c.cyan>It could have. There was a moment in there
where I'd have admitted to anything.</c>

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:07.940 line:91%
Was it the moment
before you saw the skeleton?

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:10.940 position:61% line:91%
<c.cyan>Yeah, the second the skeleton happened,
I was like, "Oh it's fine."</c>

00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:14.300 line:91%
<c.yellow>Yeah, it was a lot scarier
before the skeleton showed up.</c>

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:16.640 line:91%
No, it didn't work. No.
I have no idea.

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:20.140 line:91%
So based purely on,
like, initial reactions,

00:06:20.140 --> 00:06:22.240 line:85%
I don't think it was you.

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:26.120 line:85%
If you two didn't split it...

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:27.940 line:85%
then I think it's Dan.

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:29.260 line:85%
Whoever stole the cookie, stand...

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:30.900 line:85%
Yes!

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:32.700 line:85%
Agh!

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:34.060 line:85%
<i>[stammers]</i>

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:37.620 line:91%
<i>I was right about one thing:
Two of them had split the cookie.</i>

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:39.880 line:85%
<i>But it was Dan and Chloe.</i>

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:42.500 line:85%
<i>This invention does not work,</i>

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:46.020 line:85%
<i>just like every other lie detector.</i>

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:48.940 position:61% line:91%
